# Chain Rules

Purpose:
  Unbreakable laws for chain execution. Flows through every node.

Rules:
  CR1: Every arm MUST return to parent D0 after completion.
  CR2: Human MUST approve before entering S1 from D1.
  CR3: Human MUST approve before entering C1 from S1.
  CR4: Token delta MUST be recorded for every stage.
  CR5: AI MUST NOT read project/ before S1 approval.
  CR6: Every output MUST be validated before returning to D0.
  CR7: If a stage fails, retry max 3 times before escalating.
  CR8: Project root is source of truth for code; .sdd is source of truth for intent.
  CR9: docs/ is human language; .sdd/project/ is AI language.
  CR10: Chain execution MUST be idempotent.

 AppliesTo: P1,D1,S1,C1,R1,DEP1

State: +
